; Two zones, delegated with opposite opinions about how long the
; delegation may be kept.
;
;   parentlong.   the parent says an hour, the zone says two seconds
;   parentbrief.  the parent says two seconds, the zone says an hour
;
; Whichever of the two numbers a resolver keeps, one of these will have
; it going back to the root after three seconds and the other will not.
;
; No DS on either: everything below is insecure, so the only thing
; whose time runs out is the delegation itself.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 3600
@			IN	SOA	ns.root. root.root. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@			IN	NS	ns.root.
ns.root.		IN	A	{{ROOT_ADDR}}
parentlong.		3600	IN	NS	ns.parentlong.
ns.parentlong.		3600	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
parentlong.		3600	IN	DS	{{DS parentlong}}
parentbrief.		2	IN	NS	ns.parentbrief.
ns.parentbrief.		2	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
parentbrief.		2	IN	DS	{{DS parentbrief}}
